@njhill — could you take a look at this PR when you have a moment?

It fixes how per-request errors surface after an engine crash: today `OutputProcessor.propagate_error()` hands the **same** `EngineDeadError` instance to every in-flight request's `RequestOutputCollector`, and each consumer's `raise` prepends its frames onto the shared `__traceback__` — so every request logs an ever-growing traceback, and log volume grows quadratically with in-flight requests (incident: 93 ever-growing tracebacks, 233→845 lines each, 41,340 ERROR lines in ~10 minutes at ~90 concurrent requests; see #56943).

The fix raises a fresh `EngineDeadError() from None` per request in `RequestOutputCollector.get()/get_nowait()` — the root cause is already logged exactly once by `AsyncLLM.output_handler`, and non-`EngineDeadError` exceptions still pass through unchanged. Rebased on latest main, DCO-clean, new unit tests pass. Thanks!

